WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.357
PARTITION BY divides rows into independent window groups.

00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:10.262
Without a partition, the window can operate over all rows.

00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:15.312
With department partitioning, calculations restart for each department.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:20.582
With patient partitioning, sequence calculations restart for each patient.

00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:27.032
Partition changes the calculation context, not the number of output rows by itself.

00:00:27.032 --> 00:00:34.432
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:34.432 --> 00:00:37.907
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:43.552
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:43.552 --> 00:00:48.080
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
